endpoints.details:
A page of the requests waiting for me (the list loads more as you scroll), with how many
of each kind wait in all. group: Leave | Expenses | Attendance | Shifts | Check-in & out;
sort: oldest (default — first come, first decided) | newest.

My expense claims. With page_length (the app loading as you scroll): {claims, has_more};
without it the newest 50 as a list (older app versions). status: Pending | Approved | Rejected |
Paid; sort: newest | oldest | amount_high.

People in the business. With page_length (the app loading as you scroll): {people, has_more}
for that page; without it, everyone as a list (older app versions). sort: name | joined |
department; app: has (signed in to the app) | none.

Business › Plans and billing: every invoice of the business that's open — apps and managed services together —
newest first, a page at a time. status: open | paid. The owner and admins get Pay now on open ones;
everyone in the business can see them.

Start an app on one of its public plans. trial=1: its free trial (once per app; the first invoice comes
before the trial ends). Otherwise a paid plan waits for its first invoice (pay_url); a free plan, or QTT's own
business, starts at once. → {status, invoice, pay_url}

Ready-written words for a design (the content library, free): ideas that suit its post types and the business's kind,
festivals coming up first, each filled from Business › Knowledge — or, when a fact is missing, what to add to use it.
{ideas: [{key, post_type, occasion, date, words, missing}], language}

Cancel at period end (default) or now. Razorpay is cancelled too;
a gateway failure is logged and caught by the nightly reconcile, the
same as a customer-initiated cancel.

The business's chats for this person: channels (open to the business, or private ones they're in), direct
messages with people in the business, each with unread, @mentions and the last message; threads with new replies;
the people with presence and status; my status; unread activity; whether the AI extras can be used.
